title: A console's tab is dragged along the row to another place: the drop line shows where it goes, letting go moves it there, the order is the one the keys go round and the one that comes back on the next start
folders: rust-small
limit: 90
expect-log: script: console tab 1 .*"uno" card 0
expect-log: script: console tab 1 .*"tres" card 0
expect-log: script: console tab 2 .*"uno" card 0
expect-log: script: console tab 3 .*"dos" card 0
expect-log: script: console tab 1 .*"tres" card 0
expect-log: script: console tab 3 .*"uno" card 0
again-expect-log: script: console tab 1 .*"tres" card 0
again-expect-log: script: console tab 2 .*"dos" card 0
again-expect-log: script: console tab 3 .*"uno" card 0
forbid-log: WARN.*script
forbid-log: console: .* did not start

wait 3000
term new bash
wait 2500
term rename uno
term new bash
wait 2500
term rename dos
term new bash
wait 2500
term rename tres
wait 800
term report
mark a-three-tabs
wait 600
term movetab 3 1
wait 1500
term report
mark b-the-last-dragged-to-the-front
wait 600
term movetab 2 end
wait 1500
term report
mark c-the-second-dragged-to-the-end
wait 500
quit

=== again
wait 4000
term report
mark d-the-order-came-back
wait 500
quit
